! P27 cure step — Opus seam lead, lane p27-wire

Controller: Lares-Kiaʻi. Worktree /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/p27-wire/wt, branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5&#45;-p27-wire, head ed44bf39a (PR #200), built. Two independent reads say HOLD; read both whole, then measure each finding before curing (pentabarf V):
* Sol design read: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/p27-wire/sol-read-verdict.md
* Blind Opus custody read: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/p27-wire/blind-opus/out.md

THE SHAPE OF THE PROBLEM: the one predicate holds; the PRODUCTION COMPOSITION (`makeHeldShareFloor` and its readers) over-refuses, and every lane witness runs on permissive stubs (`publicShareTiers`, `federatable: () => true`), so nothing tested what ships. Landing as is would stop public boards reaching the world, sibling devices syncing, browser leaf ↔ hearth relay and herm /cas: the household walk (M3) would break.

CURE (end state, no back-compat, refusals by name, no implicit empty fallbacks):
# Secrets scope: read the registry through `faceScopedSecrets(registry.plane, ownsDoc)` with a PROVEN ownership reader (unresolved ownership still refuses); wire `registry.initialize()` durably where the sealed face catalog binds (open-node-vessel ~:2657 / face creation), never an implicit empty registry; registration waits for a secrets store (the operator's parked vault) and stays unwired.
# The structural floor reads the gate that actually allowed the share (selfSlotFedGate, the sibling gate, `crossing.gate`), not a fresh DeterministicFederationGate holding only the five public boards; the face-grant ring proves `fleet`; canon, persona planes and face-grant planes reach their audiences.
# Non-bag planes (the face catalog `…/bags/catalog/face`, hosting docs) bind as `{kind:"non-bag"}` with an explicit declared floor; contracted carriers get CONTRACT.
# Herm /cas checks the board id that carries the reference and every doc `documentsForCid` returns (`tiers.require(id,"world")`); the floor porch's released-floor serve passes the predicate; realm books keep their document binding (Sol F4).
# Browser audience: positive house-peer membership and positive fleet proof; an unclassified peer or null-gate relay refuses by name (Sol P1 #2; blind F9b).
# P2s: a present `null` refinement parses (VEIL), only `undefined` reads absent (share-tighten ~:135); node session CAS refusals carry the refusal field (worker-handle ~:119) and reject through `vesselCasAsker`; plugin CIDs that plugin resolution proved count as references (blind F5), and a browser replica without a genesis seed still loads its engine; non-session wiki islands get the gated sync leg sessions get (`view.attach`) so one island cannot forge its plane (blind F6), or, if that is too large for this step, name it as an owed row with its scenario; stop passing CAS dirs to node workers (Sol P3, blind F8) and state the OPFS same-origin limit in the claim.
# THE HONEST WITNESS (required): tests that run the REAL `makeHeldShareFloor` composition with production-shaped readers (no permissive stub): crossroads reaches `world`; a sibling device reads a `personagroup` plane at `fleet`; a fresh bound face catalog shares after init; an unproven browser peer refuses; a private blob stays refused to `world` while the face's daemon island reads it `in-process`. Also run (lead runs, single file, bwrap) the existing P27 manifest: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-joshu-Synthetic-Dream-Machine/eb8cf0a6-ccb1-4c58-8740-6730b6fd611d/scratchpad/p27-files.txt (browser-package files ride CI).

LAW: red first with a control for each cure; daemon packages single files only, `bwrap --dev-bind / / --unshare-pid --proc /proc --die-with-parent`, NODE_OPTIONS=&#45;-max-old-space-size=1536, scratch HOME + LAR_ROOT, LAR_BAGS unset; `pnpm build` in the lane before tests read dist; the pre-push gate. Never write or pnpm install in /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine. Commit red then cure with `git commit -F <msgfile> --only -- <paths>`, subject `lar:///w1.w2.w3 — summary`, ending:
